Subject: [PATCH] Admin: Product lab, and 300 synthetic personas for AI-run
 research

The sidebar group Product is now Product lab (User journey, Personas).

Personas (/admin/personas, staging only via RELEASES.personas): 300
synthetic people generated from a fixed seed, so everyone sees the same
ones and a panel can be re-run exactly. Rules keep each one coherent: age
fits work and household; goal fits struggle, triggers and the user-journey
moments they would hit; distrust of AI shows up as a barrier; someone who
never meditated uses no app. Variety covers six goals, ages 18-82, 17
countries, nine work patterns, four meditation and four AI attitudes,
income and willingness to pay, privacy, preferences, and circumstances to
test for (low vision, ADHD, shift work, bereavement, burnout and more).

The page shows the mix, a searchable table, and a side panel per persona
with a role-play prompt that says it is synthetic. Draw a research panel
balances goals and is reproducible from its number; it exports with a
prompt per persona. Data and helpers in admin/data/personas.ts, tested.

